{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לשכן שמו שם שמה", :translit "l'shachen sh'mo sham shamah", :gloss "to cause His name to dwell there, there"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "the doubled word שם/שמה hints to two distinct courtyards for two tiers of offerings"}], :frame {:text "The verse says לשכן שמו שמה, employing both שם (there, masculine) and שמה (there, feminine) for a single location. This verbal redundancy is read as alluding to two distinct sacred zones: one for kodshei kodashim (most holy offerings, consumed within the sanctuary building) and one for kodshim kalim (lesser holy offerings, slaughtered in the outer courtyard), reflecting the spatial hierarchy described in the Temple layout (Middot 2:3; Zevachim 5:1–7).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 12:11" "Middot 2:3" "Zevachim 5:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "the doubled word שם/שמה hints to two distinct courtyards for two tiers of offerings", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:09.182249422Z", :model "glm-5.2"}